    {
      "id": "block-adamw-update-card",
      "kind": "card",
      "level": "remembering",
      "locator": "§2, Algorithm 2",
      "front": "What does the “W” change in AdamW?",
      "back": "Weight decay is applied directly to the parameters, separately from Adam’s moment-normalized loss-gradient step. AdamW does not add λθ to the gradient before Adam adapts it.",
      "latex": "\\theta_t=\\theta_{t-1}-\\eta_t\\left(\\alpha\\frac{\\hat m_t}{\\sqrt{\\hat v_t}+\\epsilon}+\\lambda\\theta_{t-1}\\right)",
      "box": 1,
      "dueAt": 1788739200000,
      "createdAt": 1788253200000,
      "updatedAt": 1788771600000
    },
    {
      "id": "block-adamw-equivalence-card",
      "kind": "card",
      "level": "remembering",
      "locator": "§2, Propositions 1–2",
      "front": "When are L2 regularization and weight decay equivalent?",
      "back": "For standard SGD, after rescaling the coefficient by the learning rate. In general they are not equivalent for adaptive methods such as Adam because the preconditioner also transforms the L2 gradient.",
      "box": 0,
      "dueAt": 1788739200000,
      "createdAt": 1788253200000,
      "updatedAt": 1788771600000
    },
    {
