    {
      "id": "block-adamw-evaluation-note",
      "kind": "note",
      "level": "evaluating",
      "locator": "§4 and experiment design notes",
      "text": "What this paper does not establish for your project\n\n• AdamW is not a guarantee of lower validation loss on every model or dataset.\n• A better training loss alone does not demonstrate better regularization.\n• One learning rate and one decay value cannot separate optimizer choice from tuning quality.\n• More optimizer steps change accumulated decay, so budgets must match.\n\nUseful verdict: “AdamW helped here” only after a matched comparison reports validation behavior, variance across seeds, and the searched hyperparameter ranges.",
      "createdAt": 1788253200000,
      "updatedAt": 1788771600000
    },
    {
      "id": "block-adamw-evaluation-table",
      "kind": "table",
      "level": "evaluating",
      "locator": "§4.1–4.3",
      "title": "Fair comparison checklist",
      "columns": [
        "Control",
        "Keep comparable",
        "Why"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Initialization",
          "Same seeds or paired initial checkpoints",
          "Reduces noise unrelated to the optimizer"
        ],
        [
          "Training budget",
          "Same updates, batches, and evaluation cadence",
          "Controls accumulated learning and decay"
        ],
        [
          "Search effort",
          "Comparable grids for learning rate and regularization",
          "Avoids giving one optimizer more tuning"
        ],
        [
          "Primary metric",
          "Held-out loss or task metric",
          "Tests generalization rather than memorization"
        ],
        [
          "Diagnostics",
          "Training loss, validation loss, parameter norms",
          "Shows where behavior diverges"
        ],
        [
          "Failure criterion",
          "Intervals overlap or gains vanish across seeds",
          "Prevents promoting a fragile result into a claim"
        ]
      ],
      "createdAt": 1788253200000,
