    {
      "id": "block-adamw-experiment-note",
      "kind": "note",
      "level": "creating",
      "locator": "Next action",
      "text": "Experiment proposal\n\nQuestion: On my current model and dataset, does decoupled decay improve held-out performance under a matched compute budget?\n\nCandidate claim: AdamW reaches a better validation metric than Adam with a coupled L2 penalty after comparable tuning.\n\nProtocol: use paired seeds; keep data order, architecture, batch size, update count, and evaluation cadence fixed; search comparable learning-rate and regularization grids; record train/validation curves and parameter norms.\n\nReject the claim if the gain is inconsistent across seeds or disappears under a fairer hyperparameter match. Promote this block to a Question or Task when ready to run it.",
